<title>UK: Booker falls as SBC Warburg cuts to &quot;hold&quot;.</title>
<headline>Booker falls as SBC Warburg cuts to &quot;hold&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Booker Plc fell on Thursday after analysts at SBC Warburg downgraded their recommendation on the British food distributor to &quot;hold&quot; from &quot;add&quot;, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 1207 GMT, Booker shares were 6-1/2p weaker at 376-1/2 on volume of 3.9 million shares.</p>
<p>Analysts at SBC Warburg were not immediately available to comment.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Marshall, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
